\ hello.ga - print a greeting
\
\ The console is attached to the up port. Each word written to it is output
\ as a byte.

: main
    up b!                  \ B addresses the console
    'message a!            \ A walks through the message
    @+ for @+ !b unext     \ the first word is the length - 1
    down b! @b             \ nothing is connected to down, so wait forever

: message 13 , "Hello, world!" 10 ,
